<title>VENEZUELA: Venezuelan oil basket rises $0.60 in wk to $16.30.</title>
<headline>Venezuelan oil basket rises $0.60 in wk to $16.30.</headline>
<dateline>CARACAS 1997-07-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>The average export price for Venezuela's basket of crude and refined products rose $0.60 to $16.30 on Friday, compared to $15.70 on July 4, the Energy and Mines Ministry said.</p>
<p>The average price for the year so far is $16.73 per barrel, the ministry statement said.</p>
<p>Venezuela's oil export price averaged $16.92 per barrel last year compared to $14.84 per barrel in 1995.</p>
<p>The Venezuelan government based its 1997 budget calculations on an average price of $14.40 per barrel and its 1998 budget proposal is based on a $15.50 per barrel target price.</p>
<p>((-- Caracas newsroom, 582 505 2600))</p>
